  "partition": {
    "harness": "A / HARNESS: own the complete new local request ledger, begin/complete/finish/snapshot oracle, actual execute/observe integration, assertion-input control, safe report persistence, lifecycle/error handling and new selected callbacks. Also inspect new app CPU callback appearing in the shared addition. Cumulative scope owns all JSON literals/coverage and remaining static count/fence/preservation changes. Cross-boundary contract: complete independent request ledger is below; cumulative reviewer checks it against the complete portable row. Portable schemas and runner response projection are reviewed by cumulative scope; actual resource materialization and serializer/types are supplied here. Check actual response vs projected control input, header privacy/order, no fabricated IDs, strict replay/state/schema gates, observer interference and cleanup/report failure retention.\n",
    "cumulative": "B / CUMULATIVE: own the complete new JSON scenario and coverage object, all three conformance TS changes and remaining app static/count/fence/preservation hunks; inspect whole-contract scope, selection/order/fanout and existing preservation reconstruction. Harness scope owns the full new runtime oracle/report/control/lifecycle code. Cross-boundary runtime contract: it checks the independent exact11-request ledger and original response schema/full Resource/retained equality before storing a baseline or applying the one second-response assertion-input change; then joins real runner IDs and47outcomes, expects7pass/1fail only in control, and persists safe actual results/cleanup. Portable assertions alone do not establish those full-body facts. Do not infer missing helper code is absent from implementation; name any critical dependency requiring source audit.\n"
  },
